+- Observed in: editable-range label fit, Sankey-flow label backdrops, and
+  Solenoid's Recharts-to-TanStack migration
+  (`src/graph/components/chartRender.tsx` `pieLabelMarks`)
 - Friction: Case 92 estimates whether an event label fits with
   `label.length * 6 + 10`; the richer Sankey case estimates backdrop width from
   the longer label/value string, font size, and a `0.58` glyph factor. Charts
   already owns renderer-aware text measurement for axes, automatic text
   margins, focus-guide labels, and treemap fit, but ordinary definitions cannot
   compose those measured bounds into a padded background or visibility rule.
+  Solenoid's pie inside-labels sit on arbitrarily colored slices; the
+  migration layered a translucent `rect` under every label, sized from
+  `name.length * fontSize * 0.6 + 6`, only to keep the text legible. The
+  built-in crosshair already solves the same legibility problem without
+  measurement by painting a stroked copy of its label underneath.
 - Current decision: keep both presentation policies explicit. Do not expose a
   raw text-measurement utility or add a Sankey-specific label DSL. The narrow
   reusable candidate is a resolved text-frame/label composite that owns text
   measurement, padding, background geometry, and optional fit visibility while
   retaining normal text channels and renderer lifecycle. Two catalog uses are
   enough to record the seam, not enough to commit its public shape.
+  Legibility alone does not need a box: `text` now accepts `halo`, which emits
+  a round-joined stroked copy of each label directly beneath it, as the
+  crosshair label does. It needs no glyph measurement, follows rotation and
+  states through the label's own key, and paints identically in SVG and
+  Canvas. The halo covers backdrops whose only job is contrast; padded boxes,
+  borders, and fit visibility remain with the framed-label candidate.
 - Verification: both cases retain their estimates beside the authored label
   presentation, and the Sankey layout itself remains fully owned by the
   existing optional primitive. A future extraction must replace both formulas
   and prove DOM, Canvas, and native measurement behavior before this finding
-  can resolve.
+  can resolve. Text tests cover the default-off halo, default and authored
+  paint, paint order, geometry parity with the label, disabled zero-width and
+  zero-opacity halos, and state styles shared with the label; SVG and Canvas
+  renderer tests prove the stroked copy paints before the label fill.
 
